<http://data.silknow.org/object/3fdbeba2-39c7-3918-912b-47add40ba1b3>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Part of a wrapped garment, woven with patterned stripes of floss silk in white, orange, red and dark blue, the end border is in dark pink striped floss silk, reversing to yellow, with patterned coloured borders on either side, and a coloured border on one side of pink, yellow and black floss silk, probably intended to be reversible."@en , "The complete object would have been intended for use as a garment, clothing."@en , "Textile, part of a silk wrapped garment, Sindh, ca. 1855."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/4bfffc9f-ef50-3132-b6c8-b97f7cea0a8a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/fb6014b5-a9f3-3615-9126-3bfd2558944e> ;
